# Unity project ignore rules.
#
# Four things are worth tracking in a Unity project:
#   Assets/          authored content and scripts
#   Packages/        manifest.json and any local packages
#   ProjectSettings/ project configuration
#
# Everything else is derived state Unity rebuilds from those. The patterns below
# are deliberately NOT anchored with a leading slash, so they match at any depth.
#
# Verify with:
#   git check-ignore -v Library

# ---- Unity generated folders --------------------------------------------
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/

# Asset meta data should be committed, but this folder is generated.
[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*

# ---- Generated IDE project files ----------------------------------------
# Unity regenerates these. Absolute paths differ per machine, so committing
# them causes constant churn.
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.slnx
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# IDE folders created by Rider, VS and VS Code
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---- OS noise ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---- Crash and diagnostic output ----------------------------------------
sysinfo.txt
crashlytics-build.properties
*.stackdump

# ---- Build artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app
symbols/

# ---- Assignment reference material --------------------------------------
# Screenshots of the course brief and pasted snippets. Personal working
# material, not project source. The requirements they contain are summarised
# in README.md.
docs/

# ---- AI agent configuration ----------------------------------------------
# Local-only. The design decisions these files contain are documented for
# humans in README.md so the whole team can read them.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.cursor/
.cursorrules
.aider*
GEMINI.md
AGENTS.md
.windsurfrules

# ---- Never commit secrets ------------------------------------------------
# Unity project settings are safe to commit, but local credentials, signing
# keys and environment overrides must never be.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
*.mobileprovision
.env
.env.*
secrets.json